WEBVTT

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:03.720
My name is Saphentite Neikes.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:08.410
I'll be in your care as of today. 
Thank you for taking me in.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.720
<i>That was how Glenn Litbeit and I met.</i>

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:23.000
<i>As the war between the monsters 
and humans continued,</i>

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:27.710
<i>I came to the Litbeit 
household as a hostage.</i>

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:33.510
<i>Glenn's father and my family 
ran an Eastern trading company,</i>

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:37.120
<i>and were secretly trying 
open a trade route.</i>

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.310
<i>I was taken hostage to ensure my 
family wouldn't betray the company.</i>

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.280
<i>The contract went as planned,</i>

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:48.460
<i>and a year later, the long war ended.</i>

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:53.560
<i>There was no longer a 
reason to hold me hostage,</i>

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.710
<i>which also meant there was no longer 
a reason for me to stay there.</i>

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:16.610
<i>Some years later, Glenn Litbeit 
would enroll at Nemea Academy</i>

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:18.920
<i>to study monster medicine.</i>

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.380
Back then, I never dreamed I'd see him again.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:34.380
I've run out of this. I should probably ask 
the doctor to get more purified water...

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.000
Yes?

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:37.940
Good morning, Sapphee!

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:41.190
You're almost out of your 
sunblock ointment, right?

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:44.990
Why, yes I am, Dr. Glenn.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:56.220
<b>Monster Girl Doctor</b>

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:19.010
Case 2      The Mermaid of the Waterways

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:22.330
I heard that it was quite common 
to find albinos among lamias.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:25.920
What did they do when they didn't have 
sufficient protection against the sunlight?

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:29.710
I've heard that they were mostly nocturnal.

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:34.430
Our skin and eyes get damaged 
quickly in direct sunlight.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:38.310
Yeah, though I guess being nocturnal 
is out of the question for you, huh?

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:42.950
Indeed. But I'm grateful that you're 
always looking out for me, Doctor.

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:51.740
When was the last time we went out together?

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:53.530
I'm so happy that we get to do this.

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:55.840
I wonder when we last went to buy supplies.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:59.040
We have been pretty busy lately.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.750
I beg your pardon, Doctor, 
but I'll be taking my leave now.

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:07.520
Sure. Thank you very much.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.320
Please enjoy the rest of your trip.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:18.930
By the way, Sapphee, just to be clear, 
we came to buy purified water today.

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:21.210
We're not buying anything extra.

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:24.050
Yes, I'm aware of that, Doctor.

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:34.570
Welcome to the Merrow Waterways.

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:37.850
Where are you two headed today?

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:41.490
Why, of course, the gift shop on the 3rd Canal—

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.240
Please take us to the 7th Canal.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:44.470
You got it.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.840
What did I just tell you, Sapphee?

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.250
I can't recall.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:58.890
This place never ceases to amaze me...

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:01.660
The Merrow Waterways.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:07.540
Yes. I heard that a substantial budget was 
used to create these waterways in Lindworm.

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:11.350
It must be a paradise for 
monsters who live in the water.

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:13.290
Monsters and humans...

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:18.540
Creating the most optimal and 
comfortable place for all races to live...

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:23.890
It wasn't just an ideal. She managed 
to see it through in ten years.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:28.500
The Lindworm City Council representative 
Lady Skadi, known as Lady Draconness.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:32.800
Please stop at the next shop.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:38.800
It's been a while.

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:46.200
Purified water, alcohol, and vinegar.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:49.100
This should hold us over for a while.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:53.820
Please stop at the gift shop next.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:56.650
So we're going after all?

00:05:56.650 --> 00:05:59.440
Well, we won't be back here for some time, right?

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:03.320
And we're here now, so it'd be a 
waste to just go straight back home.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:05.600
Well, I guess you have a point.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:11.850
Wow, look at those 
Merrow glass works, Doctor!

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:14.590
Why don't we buy some new drinking glasses?

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:16.850
Oh! And look at those candelabras!

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:18.220
How beautiful!

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:20.430
S-Sapphee, calm down...

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:22.600
How could I possibly stay calm?

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:25.560
Buying items at the Waterways 
is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity!

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:29.870
Just like water never flows backwards, 
you only get one chance to buy things here!

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:32.520
I must take full advantage of this opportunity!

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:50.840
And after all that, that's all you bought?

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:51.630
Yes.

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:54.910
There were many other wonderful things...

00:06:55.820 --> 00:07:00.890
But the greatest gift of all is that I got to go 
shopping with you at the Waterways, Doctor.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:04.660
Well, I'm glad I could help.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:09.110
It doesn't look like there are many gondolas 
that can take us home at this hour.

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:13.030
Well, there is a mermaid show at night.

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:14.850
A mermaid show?

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:17.670
Yes. It's something that just started recently.

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:23.140
We light up the backstreets, 
and mermaids sing and dance.

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:25.580
It's a pretty popular show.

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:28.350
Lights...

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:29.410
Sapphee.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:34.430
We've got quite a haul today, so let's head 
straight home without making any detours.

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:36.950
Next time, okay?

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:39.430
Oh, all right.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:47.680
Hey! You guys on that gondola! Hold up a sec!

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.410
Are you talking to us?

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:50.440
Yeah, you!

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:55.460
The obviously beautiful couple 
over there! Come by my shop!

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:58.980
She just called us a couple! 
She's making me blush.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:01.220
Hey, pretty lamia lady!

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:04.050
You're, like, perfect for that handsome guy!

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:06.250
You're a great wife and an even better mother!

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.410
Dr. Glenn, let's stop by.

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:10.450
This mermaid is obviously a very good girl.

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:13.350
Uh, you realize that you're 
neither a wife nor a mother, right?

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:18.040
I held back on the mermaid show! 
Stopping by for a little while won't hurt!

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:20.030
All right, all right...

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.900
Welcome to my shop!

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:25.760
I'm Lulala Heine! Pleased to meet ya!

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:28.530
So, what do you sell at your shop?

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.960
Well, my singing, of course!

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:34.400
One song is only three coppers! 
Whaddya say? That's a great deal, right?

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:37.640
I see. A mermaid's song...

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:39.920
What do you think, Dr. Glenn?

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:45.040
Wha— Sapphee!

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:48.440
You have some nerve staring at 
a mermaid girl as young as her.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:51.360
What could you possibly be thinking?

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:53.300
No, that's not what I was—

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:56.070
She does have a very nice tan.

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:58.720
I guess you prefer that to 
a woman who's ghostly pale

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:00.720
because she can't be in the sun for long.

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:02.890
I never said anything like that!

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:06.560
Hey, so, uh... Are you guys 
even listening to me?

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:09.350
Oh, yeah! Hey, did you know?

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:13.260
This stone bridge is also 
known as the Lovers' Bridge.

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:17.150
During the war, a human and a mermaid jumped 
from the bridge so they could be together,

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:19.160
and then committed suicide together.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:22.740
Which means lovers can be blessed here!

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.730
Blessed because they 
committed suicide? Seriously?

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:27.760
Oh, how romantic...

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:28.500
What?

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:33.570
So if you listen to my love song here, 
your relationship will be all lovey-dovey!

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:36.130
You guys will be a couple forever!

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:38.490
So how about it? Wanna hear me sing?

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.330
Lovey-dovey...

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:45.180
Sapphee.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:46.410
Doctor?

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:47.520
I'll take care of this.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:49.410
My...

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:50.410
Lulala.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.890
I'll buy one of your songs.

00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:55.110
There's actually enough for two.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:57.620
Yay! Thanks a bunch!

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:01.120
Wait. There's only enough for one!

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:05.380
Don't make fun of me. 
My voice is worth more than that.

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:09.750
The other day, Lady Draconness 
herself came to see me!

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:14.040
She scouted me and asked if I'd 
sing at the Central Council Hall.

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:17.210
Yet you're trying to rip me off.

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:18.780
Sorry, that was unclear.

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:22.230
I meant that I'll pay for the 
other song in a different way.

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:23.940
I'll examine you.

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:25.540
Examine me?

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:27.780
Who are you guys?

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:30.690
We're from the Litbeit Clinic.

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:32.320
Clinic?

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:37.750
And this is Glenn Litbeit. 
He's a doctor who specializes in monsters.

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:41.480
You're a doctor?

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:44.990
<b>Monster Girl Doctor</b>

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:06.380
Wow.

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:11.760
No wonder she was asked to sing 
at the Central Council Hall.

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:22.280
Are you all right?

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:23.630
I'm sorry.

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:27.020
This shouldn't be happening...

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:33.550
To make up for it, I'll sing... 
from the beginning again.

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:35.480
No, that's enough.

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:37.410
Just as I promised,

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.600
I'll go ahead and examine you.

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:44.060
Sir, could you take us someplace 
where there aren't a lot of people?

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:45.290
Leave it to me!

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:48.730
Examine me?

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:59.820
The current seems much more rapid here.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:05.110
Yes. We'll be washed away if I'm not careful, 
but no other boats should come by.

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:08.140
Please take all the time you 
need for the exam, Doctor.

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:09.330
Thank you very much.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:12.740
Um... There's nothing wrong with me.

00:12:12.740 --> 00:12:16.800
I don't have any money, 
and I stopped in the middle of my song...

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:20.080
You already paid more 
than enough for the exam.

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:24.060
Your song is worth far 
more than three coppers.

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:27.990
Well, I guess if it's for free...

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:29.560
First, could you open your mouth for me?

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:30.710
'Kay.

00:12:38.370 --> 00:12:40.400
<i>There's definitely some inflammation.</i>

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:43.320
<i>She's been enduring this pain as she sang?</i>

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:46.610
Next, I need to see your chest.

00:12:46.610 --> 00:12:47.460
My chest?!

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:50.330
No! That's embarrassing...

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:52.840
Doctor, you really need to think 
about how you word things.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:56.100
Sorry. I just need to hear your breathing.

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:58.080
Well, I guess that's okay...

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:03.540
Take a deep breath.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:09.040
<i>I don't hear any problems in her breathing,</i>

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:12.010
<i>so the problem isn't in her lungs or trachea.</i>

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:15.110
Next, I need to see your gills.

00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:16.910
Uh, okay...

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:21.640
<i>When in water, mermaids normally 
breathe using their gills,</i>

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:24.480
<i>and then switch to their 
lungs when they're on land.</i>

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:28.990
<i>So why are her gills open 
even though she's on land?</i>

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:32.760
Is it all right if I touch them?

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:34.980
Sure...

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.050
Does it hurt at all?

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:41.390
It doesn't hurt, but it feels sorta hot...

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:44.970
Sorry, I promise this will be over soon.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:47.830
Humans have a higher body 
temperature than mermaids.

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:56.820
I'm going all the way in.

00:13:56.820 --> 00:13:57.920
Huh?! Wai—

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:05.520
<i>They're not secreting enough mucous.</i>

00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:09.420
<i>That's exposing the insides of her 
gills to the air, drying them out</i>

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:11.240
<i>and causing this inflammation.</i>

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:15.030
That feels weird...

00:14:15.030 --> 00:14:17.510
Just hold on a little longer, okay?

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:19.830
I'll try...

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:22.640
<i>The inflammation in her throat or 
the inflammation in her gills...</i>

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:24.600
<i>Which one's the primary cause of this?</i>

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:28.210
<i>If the problem is in her throat, 
then her lungs should be affected, too.</i>

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:29.960
<i>Which means...</i>

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:38.970
<i>The primary cause must be...</i>

00:14:45.850 --> 00:14:50.190
Lulala, how much time do 
you spend on land per day?

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:56.240
Um... Well, while the sun is up, I wait by 
the bridge to try to bring in customers.

00:14:57.630 --> 00:15:01.030
So you only spend about a quarter 
of the day in the water?

00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:02.680
I guess so?

00:15:02.680 --> 00:15:04.060
That's not good.

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:07.720
Mermaids are adapted to spend time 
both on land and in the water,

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:09.920
but primarily, they're water-based monsters.

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:12.190
For you to be on land that long is equivalent

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:16.720
to a human singing continuously in a 
desert without drinking a drop of water.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:18.670
Yeah, but...

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:21.590
It's too dangerous for you to keep that up.

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:23.980
Why do you put yourself through that?

00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:27.690
Because I don't have 
any money, obviously!

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:32.110
My dad swam off somewhere, 
leaving just my mom to take care of us!

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:36.470
I'm the oldest of four siblings, 
so I have to work hard!

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:40.780
The Waterways get a lot of customers, 
so I have to use my voice to make money.

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:42.270
Or we won't—

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:45.010
Lulala!

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:47.350
I'm sorry... I...

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:50.070
It's all right. The doctor isn't mad at you.

00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:55.870
If I can sing in the Central Council Hall, 
I'll be able to earn a salary.

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:59.460
But until then, I have to 
make money in the Waterways.

00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:01.720
I have to sing...

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.080
I'll tell you the results of your exam.

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:09.080
Lulala, your condition is caused by 
inflammation in your gills, and—

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:11.990
Johann!

00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:13.910
Mommy!

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:16.310
Someone, please!

00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:17.740
Sir, can you head over there?

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:21.370
I can't. If I go over there, 
this gondola will be washed away.

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:23.510
I'll go!

00:16:23.510 --> 00:16:24.500
Lulala?!

00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:32.510
Can you get us to the shore?

00:16:41.090 --> 00:16:44.230
<i>I have to save him! 
I have to save that little boy!</i>

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:51.820
Johann! Johann!

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:54.550
Don't worry. I'm sure he'll—

00:17:02.610 --> 00:17:03.830
Johann!

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:07.950
We need to do CPR right away!

00:17:22.300 --> 00:17:23.980
Johann? Johann!

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:27.840
Since he woke up immediately,

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:30.130
you shouldn't have to worry 
about any aftereffects.

00:17:30.130 --> 00:17:33.640
Just to be sure, please have him seen by 
a doctor who specializes in humans.

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:34.620
Thank you.

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:36.650
Thank you so much!

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:42.460
Doctor, I don't see Lulala anywhere!

00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:50.640
Doctor Glenn?!

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:57.470
Please go after the doctor!

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:04.870
<i>There have been cases in which 
mermaids drowned before.</i>

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:07.980
<i>Most of them resulted from some 
kind of ailment in their gills,</i>

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:11.260
<i>which rendered them unable to switch 
from lung breathing to gill breathing.</i>

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:17.380
<i>Lulala accidentally used her 
lungs to breathe underwater.</i>

00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:21.490
<i>Which means the water that went into her 
mouth wouldn't be expelled from her gills,</i>

00:18:21.800 --> 00:18:23.240
<i>but rather, fill her lungs.</i>

00:18:25.740 --> 00:18:28.750
<i>I can't breathe... I can't breathe.</i>

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:34.890
<i>I was so close to helping my mom out...</i>

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:38.640
<i>No... I don't want this!</i>

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:41.910
<i>Someone, please... help me...</i>

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:43.660
<i>I promise I'm going to save you.</i>

00:18:54.260 --> 00:18:56.000
<i>The channel inside Lulala...</i>

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:58.460
<i>I have to clear the way 
so water can get through.</i>

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:00.440
<i>If I can do that,</i>

00:19:00.440 --> 00:19:03.640
<i>she should be able to switch over 
to breathing through her gills...</i>

00:19:08.170 --> 00:19:09.270
<i>There.</i>

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:27.900
Sapphee?

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:33.060
I must say, it wasn't easy to 
lift you both out of the water.

00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:35.240
You're a lifesaver.

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:38.400
Honestly... You just dove right 
in without saying a word.

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:40.530
I wish you'd consider how 
I feel once in a while.

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:41.670
Sorry.

00:19:41.670 --> 00:19:43.900
You can lecture me all you want later.

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:46.470
Lulala, are you hurt anywhere?

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:49.150
Huh? No, I'm not...

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:52.590
How long must you keep hugging each other?

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:53.290
S-Sorry!

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:54.630
Get away from her, please!

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:55.710
I was just worried about her!

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:57.430
That's a completely separate matter!

00:19:57.430 --> 00:19:57.790
Uh...

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:35.280
Thank you! Thank you, everyone!

00:20:35.280 --> 00:20:39.160
I'll be singing again at noon, 
so please, come listen to me again!

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:40.850
That was such a pretty song.

00:20:40.850 --> 00:20:42.210
She was so good.

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:46.460
Hello, Lulala.

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:52.480
Miss Sapphee! And... Dr. Glenn.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:55.810
How have you been feeling?

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:58.010
Have you been using the 
moisturizer we gave you?

00:20:58.010 --> 00:21:00.470
Yeah! I've been doing great because of that!

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:04.480
I've also been sucking on the cough 
drops you gave me before I sing.

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:08.170
I promise I won't cause 
you any more trouble...

00:21:08.170 --> 00:21:09.660
like last time...

00:21:10.150 --> 00:21:11.710
What's the matter, Lulala?

00:21:11.710 --> 00:21:13.650
N-Nothing!

00:21:13.650 --> 00:21:16.160
Can you blame her for reacting this way?

00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:17.790
It may have been an emergency,

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:21.200
but you still had the nerve to do something 
like that to a young girl like her.

00:21:21.200 --> 00:21:22.980
I guess you have a point...

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:24.390
Th-That's not it!

00:21:24.860 --> 00:21:27.540
I'm really grateful to you, Doctor!

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:30.500
It's all thanks to you that 
I can sing now, and...

00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:31.630
So...

00:21:32.210 --> 00:21:33.690
So...

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:35.140
Um...

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:39.160
I'm also relieved that 
you're all right, Lulala.

00:21:48.920 --> 00:21:51.550
I wonder if she really hates me now...

00:21:51.550 --> 00:21:53.210
Who knows?

00:21:53.210 --> 00:21:54.030
Huh?

00:21:54.030 --> 00:21:56.550
I consider Lulala like a little sister,

00:21:56.550 --> 00:22:01.460
so I'd like for you two to be 
on somewhat friendly terms.

00:22:02.860 --> 00:22:04.340
"Somewhat," huh?

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.970
Case 3       The Flesh Golem Who Hates Doctors

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:39.240
Case 3: "The Flesh Golem Who Hates Doctors."
